+# ::a1 The best ice cream flavour is chocolate
+
+::a2 This is a constructed debate, made to demonstrate and test the platform for the case of many participating parties and a great depth of answers.
+
+::a3 Every summer the same argument breaks out in our office kitchen, and every summer it ends without anyone changing their mind. ::a4 I would like to make the case properly this time. ::a5 Chocolate is the best ice cream flavour, and the reasons for it are not purely a matter of taste. ::a6 A flavour can be judged by three things, namely whether it is reliable, whether it combines well with others, and whether it survives the walk home from the shop. ::a7 Chocolate wins on all three counts, and I will take them in turn.
+
+::a8 Reliability first. ::a9 A scoop of chocolate tastes roughly the same in a cheap corner shop and in an expensive gelateria, which is emphatically not true of strawberry. ::a10 Strawberry depends entirely on the fruit, and outside of about six weeks in early summer that fruit simply is not there. ::a11 Pistachio has the opposite problem. ::a12 When it is good it is extraordinary, but most of what is sold as pistachio is dyed almond paste. ::a13 Chocolate has a floor that the other flavours do not have.
+
+::a14 The second point is about combination. ::a15 Chocolate sits next to almost anything without fighting it, which is why it ends up in every mixed cup that leaves the counter. ::a16 The third point is the most practical one. ::a17 Chocolate melts slowly and stays edible, whereas a fruit sorbet turns into coloured water within minutes. ::a18 I am aware that none of this will convince the vanilla faction, but I would at least like to hear a better argument than "vanilla goes with everything".
